 6. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 A conceptual look at a BWXT Advanced Nuclear Reactor, or BANR. Photo: Courtesy of BWXT

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 ☢️ BWXT's experience with the U.S. Army's Pele project will inform its Janus work at Fort Campbell , Kentucky, where the company is expected to build and operate BANR, a high-temperature, gas-cooled nuclear reactor that uses tri-structural isotropic fuel, Joe Miller, president of government operations, told me.

 Why it matters: A quick turnaround is expected. Groundbreaking could happen as soon as 2028, with reactor operations kicking off in the early 2030s. 💭 My thought bubble: How much do y'all know about Pele? Worth a deep dive? Let me know! 🔥 Firehawk went 6-for-6 in live-fire testing of Hydra-70 rockets at Yuma Proving Ground, Arizona. The rockets were fired from an M261 launcher, seen aboard Apache , Black Hawk and Viper helicopters.

 Why it matters: "America and its allies need additional production capacity," CEO Will Edwards said in a statement. "And they need modern manufacturing approaches that can bring that capacity online faster." 💭 My thought bubble: The firing footage is worth a watch. Check that out, here . 🌊 Regent Craft, the Seaglider developer, raised $240 million, a mix of equity and debt. The Series B was co-led by Mare Liberum and AE Ventures. Debt capital was provided by Erebor Bank.

 Why it matters: "This investment marks a critical inflection point for Regent as we move from development into production," CEO Billy Thalheimer said in a statement. 💭 My thought bubble: Yes, Palmer Luckey's Erebor Bank. 🏧 The U.S. Air Force awarded $766 million in contracts for B-52 Stratofortress upgrades on Aug. 25 . RTX secured a deal for new AN/APQ-188 radars, while Boeing secured a deal for bomb rack modernization system kits.

 Why it matters: Big money. Big plane. Big lifespan. 💭 My thought bubble: Michael Marrow at Breaking Defense has much more detail, here . 
 
